### Tested versions

- Reproducible in 4.7.2.stable.mono (source inspected for the same tag)
- Code path unchanged in the current `master` at the time of writing

### System information

Godot v4.7.2.stable.mono - Android 11 - Vulkan (Mobile) - Adreno 615 - Samsung Galaxy Tab S5e (SM-T720), Snapdragon 670

### Issue description

In `RenderingDeviceDriverVulkan::swap_chain_create()` the three `swappy_mode` values are mapped to Swappy calls in an order that contradicts their own names. Values `0` and `2` are swapped.

`drivers/vulkan/rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp` (4.7.2-stable):

```cpp
enum SwappyModes {
    PIPELINE_FORCED_ON,
    AUTO_FPS_PIPELINE_FORCED_ON,
    AUTO_FPS_AUTO_PIPELINE,
};

switch (swappy_mode) {
    case PIPELINE_FORCED_ON:
        SwappyVk_setAutoSwapInterval(true);
        SwappyVk_setAutoPipelineMode(true);
        break;
    case AUTO_FPS_PIPELINE_FORCED_ON:
        SwappyVk_setAutoSwapInterval(true);
        SwappyVk_setAutoPipelineMode(false);
        break;
    case AUTO_FPS_AUTO_PIPELINE:
        SwappyVk_setAutoSwapInterval(false);
        SwappyVk_setAutoPipelineMode(false);
        break;
}
```

Per `thirdparty/swappy-frame-pacing/swappyVk.h`, both setters take "True means enable, false means disable":

```
/** @brief Enables Auto-Swap-Interval feature for all instances. */
void SwappyVk_setAutoSwapInterval(bool enabled);

/** @brief Enables Auto-Pipeline-Mode feature for all instances. */
void SwappyVk_setAutoPipelineMode(bool enabled);
```

So the current mapping means:

| `swappy_mode` | Name | Auto swap interval (auto FPS) | Auto pipeline | Actually is |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | `pipeline_forced_on` | enabled | **enabled** | auto FPS + auto pipeline |
| 1 | `auto_fps_pipeline_forced_on` | enabled | disabled | correct |
| 2 | `auto_fps_auto_pipeline` | **disabled** | disabled | pipeline forced on, no auto FPS |

`0` enables auto pipeline mode although its name says the pipeline is forced on, and it enables auto FPS although its name does not mention it. `2` disables both although its name promises auto FPS and auto pipeline. Case `1` is the only one that matches its name.

The expected mapping, keeping the names, would be:

```cpp
case PIPELINE_FORCED_ON:
    SwappyVk_setAutoSwapInterval(false);
    SwappyVk_setAutoPipelineMode(false);
    break;
case AUTO_FPS_PIPELINE_FORCED_ON:
    SwappyVk_setAutoSwapInterval(true);
    SwappyVk_setAutoPipelineMode(false);
    break;
case AUTO_FPS_AUTO_PIPELINE:
    SwappyVk_setAutoSwapInterval(true);
    SwappyVk_setAutoPipelineMode(true);
    break;
```

This matters because `swappy_mode` defaults to `2`, so projects that never touch the setting run with auto FPS *disabled* while the setting tells them the opposite, and anyone who selects `pipeline_forced_on` to avoid automatic frame-rate downshifts gets exactly the behaviour they were trying to avoid.

### Steps to reproduce

The swap is visible in the source above without running anything. It also shows up on device.

We measured presentation on a Galaxy Tab S5e using `adb shell dumpsys SurfaceFlinger --latency` (comparing `desiredPresent` against `frameReady`, so "rendered in time but presented late" is distinguishable from "not rendered in time"), with a scene whose GPU time we varied between 8 and 14 ms:

- `swappy_mode = 0` (`pipeline_forced_on`): drops to a 30 fps presentation grid at ~13 ms GPU time and does not return — the behaviour of auto swap interval being **enabled**.
- `swappy_mode = 1`: same downshift, also at ~9 ms in one of two runs.
- `swappy_mode = 2` (`auto_fps_auto_pipeline`, the default): never downshifts in any run — the behaviour of auto swap interval being **disabled**.

That is the inverse of what the names predict, and it matches the code above exactly.

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

N/A — the defect is in the mapping shown above and needs no project to observe. The device measurement is supporting evidence; the raw per-frame data is available if useful.

Possibly related: #109251.
